The test case `testQueryApiKeyWithProfileUid` is quite comprehensive, but there are a few areas that could be improved for clarity and maintainability:
1. The creation of `profileUids` can be simplified to avoid nested conditionals.
2. The handling of the `withProfileUid` parameter in the request can be made more explicit.
3. The parsing and validation of the response can be broken down into smaller, more readable methods.
Here are some suggestions for improvement:
1. Simplify the creation of `profileUids`:
```java
final List<String> profileUids = randomBoolean() ? null : List.of(randomBoolean() ? null : randomAlphaOfLength(8));
```
2. Make the handling of `withProfileUid` more explicit:
```java
Map<String, String> params = new HashMap<>();
params.put("with_profile_uid", Boolean.toString(isQueryRequestWithProfileUid));
```
3. Break down the parsing and validation of the response into smaller methods:
```java
private void assertApiKeyResponse(RestResponse restResponse, ApiKey apiKey1, List<String> profileUids) throws IOException {
    assertNotNull(restResponse);
    assertThat(restResponse.status(), is(RestStatus.OK));
    try (XContentParser parser = createParser(XContentType.JSON.xContent(), restResponse.content())) {
        Map<String, Object> queryApiKeyResponseMap = parser.map();
        assertApiKeys(queryApiKeyResponseMap, apiKey1, profileUids);
    }
}
private void assertApiKeys(Map<String, Object> responseMap, ApiKey apiKey1, List<String> profileUids) {
    assertThat((List<Map<String, Object>>) responseMap.get("api_keys"), iterableWithSize(1));
    Map<String, Object> apiKeyResponse = ((List<Map<String, Object>>) responseMap.get("api_keys")).get(0);
    assertThat(apiKeyResponse.get("id"), is(apiKey1.getId()));
    assertThat(((List<Object[]>) apiKeyResponse.get("_sort")), contains("last"));
    assertProfileUid(apiKeyResponse, profileUids);
}
private void assertProfileUid(Map<String, Object> apiKeyResponse, List<String> profileUids) {
    if (profileUids != null && profileUids.get(0) != null) {
        assertThat(apiKeyResponse.get("profile_uid"), is(profileUids.get(0)));
    } else {
        assertThat(apiKeyResponse.get("profile_uid"), nullValue());
    }
}
```

